    {
      "short": "Scale up",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "title": "Vertical scaling & the single-server ceiling",
      "body": [
        "Your first bottleneck was raw capacity: one small server has a hard requests-per-second ceiling, and queueing theory makes latency explode <em>before</em> you hit it — at ~80% utilization, wait times are already climbing fast.",
        "Upgrading the instance (<span class=\"term\">vertical scaling</span>) is the right first move: zero architectural change, immediate headroom."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "insight",
        "text": "At ~80% utilization, wait times are already climbing fast — latency explodes before capacity runs out."
      },
