    {
      "short": "The cost",
      "chapter": "tradeoff",
      "title": "What vertical scaling costs you",
      "body": [
        "Vertical scaling: simple, instant, no code changes — but notice the price curve: each tier costs roughly double for less-than-double capacity, and there is always a biggest box.",
        "Keeping ~30% headroom costs money but buys you survival during spikes you didn't predict."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "~ Instance tier: small → XL",
        "~ Cost roughly doubled for less than double the capacity",
        "~ Still a single point of failure — one box, one ceiling"
      ],
